.TH DANBY-FIREWORKS 1
.SH NAME
danby-fireworks \- launch, timed burst, and fragment trajectories
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/fireworks
.SH MODEL
Four coincident fragments first rise as one shell.  A narrow smooth impulse at
the selectable fuse time supplies the requested radial burst velocity while
preserving continuous ODE integration.  Gravity and quadratic drag then shape
each fragment trajectory.
.SH DISPLAY
The points separate visibly at ignition.  Mean altitude and horizontal spread
are plotted, making burst timing and symmetry measurable.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/danby/fireworks.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR mechanism (2)
